💥 Real Kubernetes Scenarios💥

Kubernetes is not just about kubectl apply, it is about digging into problems when things go sideways. These are real incidents you will run into, and the quick checks I run first.

⚙️ 1️⃣ CrashLoopBackOff
 Your pod keeps restarting and never stays up.
 → Check logs: kubectl logs <pod>
 → Describe the pod: kubectl describe pod <pod>
 → Look for failed init containers or configuration errors

🕵️‍♀️ 2️⃣ Deployment Rollout Stuck
 Your new version never completes rollout.
 → Check rollout status: kubectl rollout status deployment/<app>
 → Verify readiness probes and resource limits
 → Look for pending pods because of node capacity

🌐 3️⃣ Service Not Reachable
 The app is running, but cannot be accessed.
 → Confirm service type: ClusterIP, NodePort, or LoadBalancer
 → Test connectivity with curl or kubectl port-forward
 → Check DNS resolution from inside pods

🧱 4️⃣ ConfigMap or Secret Not Updated
 You changed a ConfigMap, but pods still use old values.
 → Remember, many config changes need a pod restart
 → Restart with: kubectl rollout restart deployment/<app>
 → Automate reloads using checksum annotations

🔥 5️⃣ High CPU or Memory Usage
 Pods are getting evicted or throttled.
 → Inspect metrics: kubectl top pods and kubectl top nodes
 → Tune requests and limits for containers
 → Look for memory leaks or inefficient workloads

🧩 6️⃣ Pending Pods
 Pods are stuck in Pending and never scheduled.
 → Check node capacity and resource requests
 → Review taints, tolerations, and node selectors
 → Verify storage class and PVC bindings if the pod needs volumes

🧭 7️⃣ Readiness and Liveness Probe Failures
 The app is running but not receiving traffic.
 → Recheck probe endpoints and timeout thresholds
 → Misconfigured probes can cause false restarts or block traffic

🧰 8️⃣ Node Unavailable
 Some pods are not scheduling on a node.
 → Run kubectl get nodes and look for NotReady status
 → Inspect kubelet logs on the node and check for resource pressure

Kubernetes skill is not about memorizing commands; it is about figuring out why something broke and how to make it resilient again. 
